.DS_Store
.pnpm-store/
.worktrees/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage

# TypeScript incremental build cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Design reference assets (comps + screenshots, not part of the app)
Design specifications summary*

# The dialectical engine workspace. Renamed from `DebateAI-V3/` on 2026-08-17;
# the rules below moved with it. Its own dialectical-engine/.gitignore covers
# the same ground relative to itself — these root rules are the belt to that
# braces, and they are the ones that caught the incidents noted below.
dialectical-engine/node_modules/
dialectical-engine/web/node_modules/
dialectical-engine/web/.next/
dialectical-engine/web/.next-dev*/

# apps/* build output. The rules above predated apps/ui (added 2026-08-10 as
# apps/v2-ui, renamed to apps/ui on 2026-08-17), so its build output was being
# tracked: 187 files / ~35 MB of webpack cache turned up in an unpushed commit.
dialectical-engine/apps/**/node_modules/
dialectical-engine/apps/**/.next/
dialectical-engine/apps/**/.next-dev*/
dialectical-engine/apps/**/.next-build*/

# Acceptance harness runtime state. `.pgdata` is a LIVE PostgreSQL data
# directory and `.pgdata-*` are local copies (recovery backups per DR-151,
# archived research corpora per DR-188). ALL of them are machine-local runtime
# state holding plaintext user debate content — never source.
#
# CATCH-ALL BY DESIGN (2026-08-17). The previous rules named only `.pgdata/`
# and `.pgdata-backup-*/`. An archive named `.pgdata-debate-091b7663-…`
# matched neither, so 1731 files / 72 MB of a real debate database were
# committed and pushed to a PUBLIC repo. Name-by-name rules failed because a
# new name is invented faster than the rule is updated. Match the prefix, not
# the naming convention — anywhere in the tree, at any depth.
**/.pgdata
**/.pgdata/
**/.pgdata-*
**/.pgdata-*/
